+## Submission and Preservation
+
+- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit revision, the system SHALL retain the complete submitted payload with its visit ID, revision ID, base revision ID, author ID, and server receipt time.
+- [ ] **REC-002**: When a record-store operation repeats an accepted idempotency key for the same authenticated actor with canonically identical request content, the system SHALL return the original result without creating another revision or resolution.
+- [ ] **REC-003**: When a record-store operation repeats an accepted idempotency key for the same authenticated actor with different canonical request content, the system SHALL reject the operation and leave the original operation and visit state unchanged.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When two valid submissions derived from the same current head are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both complete revisions and make the second committed revision a competitor of the first.
+- [ ] **REC-007**: The record store SHALL retain every accepted revision as an immutable complete visit payload and SHALL NOT combine fields from different revisions.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When a submission creates a visit, the system SHALL require a null base revision ID and a previously unused visit ID.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a submission edits an existing visit, the system SHALL require a base revision belonging to that visit and a plot UUID equal to the initial revision's plot UUID.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: If a submission fails validation, then the system SHALL store no revision and reserve no idempotency key for that request.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When concurrent requests use the same actor and idempotency key, the system SHALL claim the key atomically with the accepted operation so that identical requests receive the original result and different requests cannot both mutate state.
+
+## Revision State
+
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When the first valid revision for a visit is accepted, the system SHALL make that revision the visit's sole current head.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a valid edit based on the sole current head is accepted, the system SHALL make the new revision the current head without creating unresolved competition.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: When a valid edit based outside the sole current head is accepted, the system SHALL make the visit unresolved with the current head and new revision as active candidates.
+- [ ] **REC-015**: While a visit is unresolved, when a valid edit is accepted, the system SHALL add the new leaf to the active candidates and remove only its base from the active head set if that base was an active head.
+- [ ] **REC-016**: When a valid edit based outside the current head is accepted after an earlier resolution, the system SHALL make exactly the current head and new leaf active candidates without reactivating closed branches.
+- [ ] **REC-017**: The record store SHALL serialize submissions and resolutions affecting the same visit in commit order.
+
+## Retrieval and History
+
+- [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL return either one complete current revision or all complete active competing revisions, with no state in which both are returned.
+- [ ] **REC-018**: When a caller retrieves a visit's candidates, the system SHALL include each candidate's base revision ID and author ID.
+- [ ] **REC-019**: When a caller retrieves current state or history, the system SHALL construct the response from one consistent database snapshot.
+- [ ] **REC-020**: When a caller retrieves visit history, the system SHALL return complete immutable revisions and resolutions, including closed branches, ordered by a per-visit monotonically increasing server sequence number.
+
+## Resolution
+
+- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves an unresolved visit, the system SHALL retain the selected revision ID, the complete settled head ID set, the coordinator's identity, and the server resolution time.
+- [ ] **REC-021**: When a coordinator submits a resolution, the system SHALL require the selected revision to belong to the expected active head set supplied with the request.
+- [ ] **REC-022**: When a valid resolution's expected head set matches the actual active head set, the system SHALL atomically select that complete revision as current and close every other active candidate.
+- [ ] **REC-023**: If a resolution's expected head set differs from the actual active head set, then the system SHALL reject the resolution without closing any candidate or reserving its idempotency key.
+- [ ] **REC-024**: If a resolution targets a visit that is already current, then the system SHALL reject the resolution without changing the visit or reserving its idempotency key.
+- [ ] **REC-025**: When a scientific correction follows a resolution, the system SHALL accept it only as a new complete authored revision with its own base revision ID.
+
+## Operation Failures
+
+- [ ] **REC-026**: If a requested visit does not exist, then the system SHALL return a not-found outcome without changing stored state.
+- [ ] **REC-027**: If a submission has an unknown base, a cross-visit base, a duplicate initial visit ID, or a changed plot UUID, then the system SHALL return a validation failure without storing a revision.
+- [ ] **REC-028**: If an operation is unauthenticated or unauthorized, then the system SHALL return an authorization failure without changing stored state and without exposing another worker's submission payload.
